# Backend (NestJS)

`backend/` owns the NestJS API and control plane.

## Responsibilities

- Auth, sessions, authorization (keep current JWT/OTP; do not redesign)
- PostgreSQL persistence
- Business rules and orchestration
- Agent enrollment validation and ingestion
- APIs for `admin-panel/` and `client/`

## Audience namespaces

- `/api/v1/public/...` — unauthenticated intake
- `/api/v1/...` — customer JWT
- `/api/v1/admin/...` — staff JWT + role/capability
- `/api/internal/agent/v1/...` — agent only

Domain modules with separate public/customer/admin controllers. No mega `AdminModule`.

## Trust boundaries

- Agents connect outbound HTTPS to NestJS only.
- UIs never talk to agents or VPS hosts.
- Follow the module/route map; do not invent conflicting URL shapes.

